{
  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The carousel implements basic interactive controls with correct native `<button>` semantics, but lacks the structural and programmatic scaffolding required for assistive technology users to understand state changes, navigate efficiently, or contextualize the widget. Automated checks will likely pass because there are no explicit violations (e.g., missing `alt`, invalid roles), but the design is incomplete per the WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern and WCAG 2.2 requirements for dynamic content communication.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**: \nBefore reading the code, I predicted:\n1. Missing `aria-live` region for announcing slide changes to screen readers.\n2. Carousel container lacks landmark/region labeling (`role=\"region\"` + `aria-label`).\n3. Indicator buttons lack programmatic active state (`aria-current` or `aria-pressed`).\n4. No keyboard navigation (arrow keys) for the carousel widget itself.\n5. Generic/dynamic `alt` text that doesn't describe image content.\n\nAll predictions materialized during investigation. The component is functionally interactive but programmatically opaque.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Findings\n*(None found. This is not a complete access blocker; issues degrade experience significantly but do not entirely block interaction.)*\n\n### Major Findings (significantly degrades experience)\n\n1. **Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic image updates**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:16-18` (`<img>` updates via React state, but no live region or programmatic announcement exists)\n   - **User Group**: Screen reader users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages), WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requires `aria-live=\"polite\"` on the slide container or a dedicated status region.\n   - **Why this matters**: When the image changes, screen reader users hear nothing. They must manually tab to the image to discover it changed, breaking the expected widget behavior.\n   - **Fix**: Wrap the `<img>` in a `<div aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\">` or create a dedicated `<div role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">` that updates with `alt` text or a descriptive label on each slide change.\n\n2. **Indicator buttons lack programmatic active state**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:31-35` (Indicators use conditional className but no ARIA state attribute)\n   - **User Group**: Screen reader & keyboard users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value), WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requires `aria-current=\"page\"` or `aria-pressed=\"true\"` on the active indicator.\n   - **Why this matters**: Screen reader users cannot determine which slide is currently displayed. Keyboard users relying on AT feedback are left guessing.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? \"page\" : undefined}` to each indicator button.\n\n3. **Missing keyboard navigation for the carousel widget**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:21-28` (Only tab-order buttons exist; no arrow key handlers)\n   - **User Group**: Keyboard-only users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard), WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern requires left/right arrow keys to navigate slides when focus is within the widget.\n   - **Why this matters**: Users must tab through all controls sequentially to change slides. This violates the expected composite widget interaction model and creates excessive tab stops.\n   - **Fix**: Add `onKeyDown` handlers to the carousel container or image wrapper. If focus is on the image container, `ArrowLeft` calls `goToPrevious()`, `ArrowRight` calls `goToNext()`. Ensure focus doesn't leave the widget during navigation.\n\n4. **Carousel container lacks landmark/region labeling**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:14` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`)\n   - **User Group**: Screen reader users\n   - **WCAG/APG Citation**: WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships), WAI-ARIA APG requires `role=\"region\"` + descriptive `aria-label` for custom interactive widgets.\n   - **Why this matters**: Screen readers announce buttons as \"Previous button, Next button\" without context. Users don't know what these controls operate on.\n   - **Fix**: Add `role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Image carousel\"` to the container div. Consider `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"` on the image wrapper per APG.\n\n### Minor Findings (friction but workaround exists)\n\n- **Generic dynamic `alt` text** (`src/BuggyCarousel.jsx:17`): `alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} ` provides no descriptive content. Screen readers will announce \"Carousel image 3\" instead of describing the visual. Fix: Pass descriptive alt text via props or generate context-aware labels. WCAG 1.1.1.\n- **Indicator buttons lack visible focus indicators** (CSS not provided, but standard `<button>` styling often omits visible outlines). Ensure `:focus-visible` meets WCAG 2.4.7 (3:1 contrast change, minimum 2px perimeter).\n\n### Enhancements (best practice not met)\n\n- Add `aria-roledescription=\"slide\"` to the image container per WAI-ARIA Slideshow pattern.\n- Consider grouping controls with `<fieldset>` and `<legend>` if this carousel is part of a larger form or data entry flow.\n- If auto-play exists in extended versions, ensure pause/resume controls are present and announced (WCAG 2.2.2).\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing (gaps, unhandled edge cases)\n\n- **Missing live region**: No mechanism announces state changes to assistive technology.\n- **Missing widget labeling**: `role=\"region\"` + `aria-label` absent from container.\n- **Missing indicator state**: No `aria-current` or `aria-pressed` on active dot/number.\n- **Missing keyboard shortcut model**: No arrow key navigation for slide transitions.\n- **Missing `aria-roledescription`**: Carousel/slide semantics not declared per APG.\n- **Missing focus management on mount**: If this carousel mounts dynamically, focus should move to the first slide or a skip link within the region.\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | HIGH | Dynamic state changes unannounced; indicators lack active state; container unlabeled |\n| Keyboard-only | MEDIUM | No arrow key navigation; tab order linear but functional |\n| Low vision | LOW | Buttons contain text labels; no contrast data provided but standard `<button>` semantics apply |\n| Cognitive | LOW | Labels are clear; interaction model is simple but lacks AT feedback for state changes |\n\n**Screen reader user**: Will hear \"Previous button, Next button\" followed by numbered buttons. When an image changes, nothing is announced. The active indicator isn't programmatically marked. Without `aria-live` and region labeling, the widget is functionally invisible to AT beyond raw DOM traversal.\n\n**Keyboard-only user**: Can tab to all controls. Must click or press Enter on Previous/Next to change slides. No arrow key shortcuts. Focus remains on the clicked button. Functional but inefficient compared to standard carousel expectations.\n\n**Low vision user**: Text labels on buttons are accessible. Indicators use numbers, which may be small depending on CSS. No contrast data provided; verify indicator active state meets 3:1 UI boundary threshold and text meets 4.5:1 normal text threshold.\n\n**Cognitive accessibility**: Clear button labels reduce cognitive load. However, lack of programmatic feedback for slide changes may cause confusion about whether navigation worked. Consistent visual + AT feedback is needed.\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\nThe component passes basic structural checks (native `<button>` elements, valid `alt` syntax) but fails the design completeness test for assistive technology. The absence of an `aria-live` region, region labeling, indicator state, and keyboard navigation model means screen reader users cannot track state changes or navigate efficiently. These are not minor polish items; they are core pattern requirements per the WAI-ARIA Slideshow specification. The verdict is **REVISE** because the interaction model must be enhanced with programmatic state communication and keyboard shortcuts before shipping.\n\n---\n\n### Open Questions (unscored)\n- Does this carousel support auto-play? If so, pause/resume controls are required (WCAG 2.2.2).\n- Are indicator buttons intended to be focusable, or should they use `tabindex=\"-1\"` with a separate focusable control group?\n- Is the `alt` text dynamic in production, or will it be passed as a prop array for accurate descriptions?\n- Does the parent application provide global skip links or landmark structure that partially compensates for this component's missing region labeling?\n\n**Mitigated by**: None. These gaps require implementation changes. The component is not blocked from shipping if used in a highly constrained context with explicit developer documentation, but it fails standard accessibility design completeness criteria.",
